From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: switch the vertical front porch in place on Baldur
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A mode that differs from the running one only in the vertical front porch
takes no full modeset on a DSI video-mode pipeline: dpu_crtc_atomic_check()
clears mode_changed and the encoder rewrites DSI_TOTAL.V_TOTAL on the DSI
hosts and INTF_VSYNC_PERIOD_F0 on the INTFs, marking them for the CTL flush.
The INTF period is double buffered and latches at the next vsync after that
flush.  ACTIVE_V, the vsync position, display_v_end and DSC do not depend on
the front porch.

This is the vendor "DFPS" refresh-rate switch.  A full modeset at 60 or 30 Hz
makes the Lenovo TB323FU CSOT NT36523 panel flicker.

Provenance: this project's Lenovo TB323FU tree at
11a25bf89b65fff48112a91a0b25bc247e7736d8, patches 0065 and 0079.  The
porch-only comparison, the DSI/INTF programming and the colour-management
guard are carried over unchanged; the only new conditions are machine gates:
both the CRTC check and the encoder update return early unless
of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,baldur"), so every other machine never
clears mode_changed, enters the update path or writes the DSI/INTF timing,
and the new callback registration alone has no effect there.  No third-party
sign-off is implied.

---
 10 files changed, 187 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)
